WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.060
Concepts, constraints, and compile-time guards help turn implicit assumptions into visible rules.

2
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:15.240
A constrained template tells callers what kinds of types are intended before the compiler tries to instantiate a large body of code.

3
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:20.220
That makes the API easier to understand and makes misuse easier to diagnose.

4
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.220
Good constraints are meaningful and specific.

5
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:30.360
A broad template that accepts almost anything may look flexible, but it is harder to review and easier to misuse.

6
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:40.140
A concept that states the required operations, value category expectations, or iterator category gives reviewers a clearer model of the intended behavior.

7
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:45.940
static_assert can enforce important assumptions that are not naturally captured by a simple expression requirement.

8
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:52.760
A template might require a type to be nothrow movable, explicitly allowed by policy, or safe for a particular storage model.

9
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.940
When a guard fails, the diagnostic should explain what the caller needs to change.

10
00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.180
Compile-time checks should not become decorative noise.

11
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.440
They should protect invariants that matter.

12
00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.820
A guard that simply repeats what the compiler would already report may not help.

13
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.560
A guard that explains the security-relevant contract can save time and prevent accidental broad use.

14
00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.400
The result is a safer failure mode.

15
00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:27.180
Instead of compiling a surprising instantiation and discovering a defect later, the code rejects unintended use early with a message connected to the template's design.

16
00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.100
Well-designed constraints also reduce review burden.

17
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:37.720
Reviewers can focus on whether the constraint matches the design rather than guessing from every operation buried inside the implementation.
